{
  "title": "[dynamo] Add most recent bytecode/Python stack context to graph break developer error context",
  "issue_id": "162858",
  "bug_description": "Log the last k (k = 50?) bytecode instructions traced, along with the state of the symbolic Python stack.\n\ni.e. print the last k outputs of `TORCH_LOGS=trace_bytecode` when logging a graph break.\n\nFor example,\n```python\nimport torch\n\n\n@torch.compile(backend=\"eager\")\ndef fn(x):\n    y = x + 1\n    z = x + y\n    torch._dynamo.graph_break()\n    return z\n\n\nfn(torch.ones(3))\n```\n\nWould have these instructions logged into the graph break message:\n```\nGraph break in user code at /data/users/williamwen/pytorch/playground3.py:8\nGraph Break Reason: Call to `torch._dynamo.graph_break()`\n  Explanation: User-inserted graph break. Message: None\n  Hint: Remove the `torch._dynamo.graph_break()` call.\n\n  Developer debug context: Called `torch._dynamo.graph_break()` with args `[]`, kwargs `{}`\n  Most recent 50 bytecode instructions traced:\n    RESUME 0 []\n    LOAD_FAST x []\n    LOAD_CONST 1 [LazyVariableTracker()]\n    BINARY_OP 0 [LazyVariableTracker(), ConstantVariable(int: 1)]\n    STORE_FAST y [TensorVariable()]\n    LOAD_FAST x []\n    LOAD_FAST y [TensorVariable()]\n    BINARY_OP 0 [TensorVariable(), TensorVariable()]\n    STORE_FAST z [TensorVariable()]\n    LOAD_GLOBAL torch []\n    LOAD_ATTR _dynamo [LazyVariableTracker()]\n    LOAD_ATTR graph_break [LazyVariableTracker()]\n    CALL 0 [LazyVariableTracker(), NullVariable]\n\n For more details about this graph break, please visit: https://meta-pytorch.github.io/compile-graph-break-site/gb/gb0025.html\nUser code traceback:\n  File \"/data/users/williamwen/pytorch/playground3.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    fn(torch.ones(3))\n  File \"/data/users/williamwen/pytorch/playground3.py\", line 8, in fn\n    torch._dynamo.graph_break()\n```\n\nIncluding bytecode source attribution to the logged VariableTrackers (https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/162857) would make this debug information even more helpful.\n\ncc @chauhang @penguinwu @voznesenskym @EikanWang @jgong5 @Guobing-Chen @XiaobingSuper @zhuhaozhe @blzheng @wenzhe-nrv @jiayisunx @chenyang78 @kadeng @amjames @Lucaskabela",
